From a1ed124baa690cfd0c60b1a09d30964b5fa9242c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChenXiaoSong <chenxiaosong@kylinos.cn>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:01:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] smb/server: validate symbolic link reparse buffers

Add strict parsing of IO_REPARSE_TAG_SYMLINK buffers before exposing
FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT. Validate lengths, offsets, flags, embedded NULs
and UTF-16 scalar values. Decode POSIX targets without changing their
separators and translate relative Windows targets to local path syntax.

Add three KUnit tests covering valid targets, malformed buffers and the
PATH_MAX boundary. No SMB command uses the parser at this stage.

Example:

  1. Enable these options in the test kernel configuration:
     CONFIG_KUNIT=y
     CONFIG_SMB_SERVER=y
     CONFIG_SMB_KUNIT_TESTS=y
     CONFIG_SMB_SERVER_KUNIT_TESTS=y
     CONFIG_TMPFS=y
     CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y
  2. Build and boot that kernel.
  3. Read its boot log:
     dmesg | sed -n '/# Subtest: ksmbd-reparse/,+9p'

     ok 1 ksmbd_symlink_parse_targets
     ok 2 ksmbd_symlink_parse_malformed
     ok 3 ksmbd_symlink_parse_length_limit
     # ksmbd-reparse: pass:3 fail:0 skip:0 total:3

Remote ln -s remains unsupported until SET is wired up later.

Code and test instructions generated with OpenAI Codex assistance.
